      "date": "1906-04-19",
      "kind": "event",
      "description": "Saved from the fire after the earthquake: before leaving, the resident publisher Edward A. Dakin dipped his largest flag in salute, which brought a company of soldiers up the hill to fight the flames with bathwater, building sand and soda siphons. It is why the house is called the House of the Flag, San Francisco Landmark No. 46.",
      "source": "nrhp-87002289"
    }
